e. Known to some as a Beaver Moon, November's Full Moon was also near perigee, the closest point in its elliptical orbit around planet Earth. That made it one of the biggest and brightest Full Moons, also known as a supermoon. In fact, November's Full Moon was the first in a series of four consecutive Full Moon's near perigee. So your next chance to watch a supermoon rise will be when the Cold Moon rises on December 23.","img":"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/november/Plenilunio1_2048r.jpg?w=1400&fit=clip","by":"Marcella Pace","video":false},"tle":["1 25544U 98067A   26330.94400774  .00010411  00000+0  19252-3 0  9997","2 25544  51.6316 214.6424 0007338  69.7098 290.4679 15.49629890596984"],"passes":[{"start":"2026-11-27T17:38:31Z","end":"2026-11-27T17:43:49Z","top":"2026-11-27T17:41:42Z","max":42,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-27T19:16:53Z","end":"2026-11-27T19:16:53Z","top":"2026-11-27T19:17:48Z","max":11,"from":["SW","西南"],"to":["SW","西南"],"mins":1},{"start":"2026-11-28T16:50:26Z","end":"2026-11-28T16:56:59Z","top":"2026-11-28T16:53:43Z","max":56,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":7},{"start":"2026-11-28T18:27:50Z","end":"2026-11-28T18:31:20Z","top":"2026-11-28T18:29:58Z","max":16,"from":["W","西"],"to":["S","南"],"mins":4},{"start":"2026-11-29T17:39:23Z","end":"2026-11-29T17:44:47Z","top":"2026-11-29T17:42:05Z","max":23,"from":["W","西"],"to":["S","南"],"mins":5},{"start":"2026-11-30T16:51:07Z","end":"2026-11-30T16:57:08Z","top":"2026-11-30T16:54:08Z","max":31,"from":["W","西"],"to":["SE","東南"],"mins":6},{"start":"2026-12-01T17:41:09Z","end":"2026-12-01T17:43:18Z","top":"2026-12-01T17:42:13Z","max":11,"from":["SW","西南"],"to":["SW","西南"],"mins":2},{"start":"2026-12-02T16:52:07Z","end":"2026-12-02T16:56:31Z","top":"2026-12-02T16:54:19Z","max":17,"from":["W","西"],"to":["S","南"],"mins":4}],"track":{"t0":"2026-11-27T07:48:00Z","step":60,"p":[[-25.5,7.4],[-22.7,10.1],[-19.8,12.6],[-16.8,15.